test_command=sh tests/receipts_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-sessionguards_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-skills-block_test.sh && sh tests/skills-activation-prompts_test.sh && sh tests/renderinject_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-render-sync_test.sh
id=receipts-01 result=green reason=unit test "receipts-01: the coder prompt states the receipt duty -- NN-<feature>.result named after the sub-spec, exactly one test_command= line with the discovered command, one id line per declared id" passes -- the coder prompt's new "## Receipt" section states the receipt path spdd/changes/<slug>/NN-<feature>.result written at the end of each session that finishes or advances a sub-spec, named after the sub-spec file (01-api.feature -> 01-api.result), exactly one `test_command=` line whose value is the unit-suite run command this session discovered and used for this sub-spec (discovery is the coder's job, the way any contributor would: a package.json test script, a Makefile test target, the language's standard convention), and one `id=` line per declared scenario id of the form id=<feature>-<index> result=<green|skip|blocked> reason=<text>
id=receipts-02 result=green reason=unit tests "receipts-02 (green row)", "receipts-02 (skip row)", and "receipts-02 (blocked row)" pass -- the receipt section's result-vocabulary list carries all three Example rows: a passing unit test records result=green reason=<unit test name>, an ordinary skip (not unit-testable, no stub) records result=skip reason=<why>, and a BLOCKED: skip/reason stub records result=blocked reason=BLOCKED: <why>
id=receipts-03 result=green reason=unit test "receipts-03: the receipt's id set equals the declared id set exactly -- scenario order, no foreign id, no silent omission" passes -- the section states each id line names a scenario id from the sub-spec's exact declared id set, each once, in the sub-spec's scenario order, with a non-empty reason; a foreign id (one the sub-spec does not declare) never appears; and a declared id with no test yet still gets its line (result=skip or result=blocked with an honest reason) -- never a silent omission
id=receipts-04 result=green reason=unit test "receipts-04: a later session rewrites the same receipt in place -- the file always holds the newest session's state" passes -- the section states a receipt already existing from an earlier session on the same sub-spec is rewritten in place -- the same file, never a second, accumulated NN-<feature>.result-2 or sibling file: the file always holds the newest session's state (its outcomes and its test command)
id=receipts-05 result=green reason=unit test "receipts-05: a planning-stage refusal still produces a truthful receipt -- every id result=blocked, the same BLOCKED: reason, test_command= never empty" passes -- the section states a planning-stage refusal (the existing whole-sub-spec BLOCKED: stub, tagged with the sub-spec's first scenario id) still produces a truthful receipt: every declared id gets result=blocked and the same `BLOCKED: <why>` reason, and test_command= still records the discovered (or honestly undiscoverable) suite command, so the receipt is never empty
id=receipts-06 result=green reason=unit tests in tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh pass (15 receipts-06 runtime cases: the pinned field order on every subspec= line; receipt=missing covered=0/N complete=no class=in_progress; all-green done; ordinary-skip done; blocked checked first regardless of coverage; blocked outranking complete; no/two/empty test_command=, foreign id, duplicate id, uncovered id, and empty reason all forcing complete=no with class=in_progress; empty ids never vacuously done), plus the pre-existing ids tests updated to the extended line -- scripts/orchestration/antz-probe.sh extends every subspec= line with receipt=<file|missing> covered=<n>/<N> complete=<yes|no> class=<done|blocked|in_progress>, complete=yes requires the receipt to exist with exactly one non-empty test_command= line and exactly the declared id set, and class= applies the mapping (any result=blocked -> blocked, checked first; else complete -> done; else in_progress); the probe's other outputs (open_questions=, rejected_count=, change_dir=missing, empty-ids report) are unchanged
id=receipts-07 result=green reason=unit test "receipts-07: the orchestrator's step 3 classifies from the probe's receipt fields alone and no longer runs the suite for classification" passes -- step 3 now opens with classification-is-file-reading from the probe's receipt fields (receipt=/covered=/complete=/class=) stated authoritative, classifies class=blocked (checked first regardless of coverage; stop at the first one found, relay its BLOCKED: reason, route it to specifier), class=done (complete=yes, every id green or ordinary-skip), and class=in_progress (delegate to a fresh coder session, one per sub-spec, sequentially never in parallel), keeps the empty-ids stop-and-ask rule (never vacuously done), and the old run-for-classification sentence ("Run it, then classify each sub-spec from its ids") is gone with the suite instructions now living only in the doubtful-receipt bullet
id=receipts-08 result=green reason=unit test "receipts-08: the doubtful-receipt exception -- one suite re-run for that doubtful sub-spec only, classified from the actual run, receipt never fabricated" passes -- step 3's final bullet covers class=in_progress with complete=no (missing, incomplete, or mismatched): re-run the unit suite once, for that doubtful sub-spec only, using the receipt's `test_command=` value when the receipt carries one, else discovering the command the way any contributor would (installing missing host-project dependencies first), classify from the actual run result (all green/ordinary-skip -> done; any BLOCKED: skip -> blocked; any red -> in_progress, delegating a fresh coder session), report the receipt doubt in the report, and never write, fix, or fabricate the receipt -- the receipt stays the coder's artifact, even when wrong
id=receipts-09 result=green reason=unit test "receipts-09: no pre-verifier gate -- step 4 routes to the verifier without running the unit suite; the verifier's e2e suite stays the independent gate" passes -- step 4 now states routing happens without running the unit suite at all (classification came from receipts; there is no "final gate" re-test) and that the verifier's own e2e Integration Verification suite remains the independent gate
id=receipts-10 result=green reason=unit tests "receipts-10: AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md carry an identical receipt-convention gotcha bullet" and "receipts-10 (gotcha updates)" pass -- both policy docs carry the byte-identical Receipts bullet (path, coder-written at session end, test_command= plus per-id result=green|skip|blocked grammar, BLOCKED: blocked reasons, classifies by reading receipts, unit suite only for a doubtful receipt, never as a pre-verifier gate), the probe gotcha's facts gain the receipt classification fields read from the coder's NN-<feature>.result receipts with discovery moved to the coder, the stale "requires actually running the unit suite" classification sentence is replaced by reads-the-receipt wording, and the REJECTED.md gotcha's stale "embedded probe script" sourcing is fixed to the scripts/orchestration/antz-probe.sh source-of-truth wording in both docs
